.TH TAXIPRIJS 1 "2024" "taxiprijs 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
taxiprijs \- Dutch taxi fare calculator TUI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taxiprijs
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B taxiprijs
is a terminal user interface application for calculating taxi fares in the Netherlands.
.PP
It supports configurable pricing for different passenger groups and uses TOML for configuration.
.PP
The main menu displays the current version and provides options for fare calculation,
settings, help, initial setup, update checking, branch switching, and uninstalling.
.SH OPTIONS
.B taxiprijs
does not take any command line options.
.SH KEYBOARD CONTROLS
.TP
.B 1
Calculate fare
.TP
.B 2
Settings
.TP
.B 3
Help/Manual
.TP
.B 4
Initial setup
.TP
.B 5
Check for updates (GitHub)
.TP
.B 6
Switch branch (dev / stable)
.TP
.B 7
Uninstall
.TP
.B q
Quit
.TP
.B Tab
Next input field
.TP
.B Shift+Tab
Previous input field
.TP
.B Enter
Submit/Save
.TP
.B Esc
Back/Cancel
.SH UPDATE & BRANCHES
The application can check for updates on GitHub and pull them directly.
.PP
Branches available:
.TP
.B dev
Development branch - may be unstable
.TP
.B v1.0.0
Stable release branch
.SH UNINSTALLING
Option 7 in the main menu starts the uninstall process.
.PP
The uninstall requires two confirmations for safety:
.IP 1. 3
First: "Are you sure you want to uninstall?" (y/n)
.IP 2. 3
Second: "WARNING: This will remove all files. Are you REALLY sure?" (y/n)
.PP
After both confirmations, the binary and desktop entry are removed via
.BR make uninstall (1).
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is stored in
.B ~/.taxiprijs/config.toml
.PP
The TOML file can be edited manually or through the Settings screen.
.PP
Example configuration:
.PP
.RS
[[passenger_groups]]
.br
name = "1-4 passengers"
.br
board_fee = 3.50
.br
per_minute = 0.50
.br
wait_minute = 0.50
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.taxiprijs/config.toml
User configuration file
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Calculate a fare:
.IP 1. 3
Start the application
.IP 2. 3
Select option 1 (Calculate Fare)
.IP 3. 3
Enter trip duration in minutes
.IP 4. 3
Enter waiting time in minutes
.IP 5. 3
Enter number of passengers (1-5)
.IP 6. 3
Press Enter to calculate
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal exit
.TP
.B 1
Error occurred
